Usage:
  feov-record [flags]
  feov-record [command]

Available Commands:
  carry           restate an earlier round's closure, when the work is done and you are not re-attesting it
  close           close a gap with the verification you did THIS round, naming what you checked it against
  closing         your closing argument on one docketed gap, when the bench is about to rule on it
  completion      Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  count-claims    count the FOOTNOTED declarative claims in blue's report (read-only)
  fetch           cached, hash-verified web read (replaces WebFetch); serves both sides the same bytes
  friction        a capability gap or protocol misfit — and the explicit empty form, for the sittings where nothing blocked you
  help            Help about any command
  inquiry-support your per-round vote on whether the report still carries a direction blue proposed
  mint            turn lens findings into a graded gap on the board, when a defect is real and belongs there
  near-match      screen a candidate against the board BEFORE minting, so a reopen does not arrive as a fresh gap
  position        your round narrative — the argument the other side answers, rendered as this round's RED section
  register        your first act at the seat, and the one call that needs your seat id — nothing else runs until it does
  regrade         move a grade on a gap that already exists, with the reason it moved
  spot-check      sample the closure archive — a duty every round owes, including the rounds with nothing to sample
  verdict         the seat's terminal act: the PASS or FAIL, and the checkpoint that follows it

Command groups — each holds commands THIS page does not list:
  class           the gap-class registry: what KINDS of defect this run recognises
  motion          file and rule on a motion — a grade dispute, a petition, or a ruling on a direction. One mechanism, one id.
  show            read a projection of the record — the tool is the read path, and the .md files are for human verification. Bare, it answers with YOUR PENDING WORK

Flags:
      --as as-value          REQUIRED — your ruling AND the gap's fate. Every value ends the gap except carried, which defers it to a later round with a stated direction. One vocabulary with red's closure classes since #342
  -h, --help                 help for opinion
      --id gap-id            REQUIRED — the gap being ruled on
      --principle string     REQUIRED — the principle applied — a ruling is an OPINION, not a disposition
      --reason string        REQUIRED — your reasoning or argument for this act — the substance the report renders and the other side answers; --reason-file for anything long or from stdin with -
      --reason-file -        read --reason from a file, or from stdin with - — the same field as --reason, for anything long or that would fight shell quoting
      --review-flag string   REQUIRED — why a human should, or should not, look at this
      --tension string       REQUIRED — the values in tension (e.g. correctness vs economy)

Enumerated values:
  --as
    closed                    the repair was verified at the leaf and nothing regressed
    closed_with_regression    repaired, but something else broke — REQUIRES a successor naming the gap that carries the regression forward
    amends_prior              a defect found BETWEEN two repairs that each closed clean earlier — REQUIRES supersedes so the lineage is explicit
    rebuttal_sustained        blue argued the finding was wrong and the argument held; nothing was repaired because nothing needed to be
    risk_accepted             the fix costs more than the defect (complexity above likelihood x impact) and the risk is taken KNOWINGLY, with the argument on the record
    routed_to_infrastructure  a real defect whose fix is owned outside this debate; it leaves here and is not silently dropped
    carried                   NOT a closure: the gap survives to the next round with a stated research direction the coming seat owes

Global Flags:
      --json             emit a structured JSON result (and structured errors) instead of human text
      --run string       the run directory. REQUIRED unless the engine injected it — it does in a real run, which is why you rarely type it. A value that DISAGREES with the run you were dispatched into is refused rather than obeyed
      --seat-id string   your seat id, assigned by the engine and bound to this role's namespace

── verdict in the wrong case
exit 2
feov-record: invalid argument "pass" for "--as" flag: --as must be one of PASS|FAIL (got "pass") — "pass" differs from "PASS" only in case, and a PASS is checked against the open board by exact match, so any other spelling skips the check entirely and records an unadjudicated pass

    PASS  every gap on the board is resolved — this is CHECKED against the open board, not taken on your word
    FAIL  at least one gap is still open, or you are not satisfied it was answered

the seat's terminal act: the PASS or FAIL, and the checkpoint that follows it

The seat's terminal act, and the checkpoint that follows it: the record is mirrored to the recovery copy.

A PASS is REFUSED while anything still blocks it — an open gap, an unruled motion, a line of inquiry unvoted this round. `show work` is the list; `sitting.complete` is true exactly when nothing blocking is left.

If you need a verb or a flag that is not listed here, it does not exist for you:
do not improvise around it, and do not hand-write the artifact. Record what you
needed and what you would have done with your role's 'friction' verb — a missing
capability is a finding about the tooling, and that channel is how it gets fixed.

