Usage:
  feov-record [flags]
  feov-record [command]

Available Commands:
  carry           restate an earlier round's closure, when the work is done and you are not re-attesting it
  close           close a gap with the verification you did THIS round, naming what you checked it against
  closing         your closing argument on one docketed gap, when the bench is about to rule on it
  completion      Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  count-claims    count the FOOTNOTED declarative claims in blue's report (read-only)
  fetch           cached, hash-verified web read (replaces WebFetch); serves both sides the same bytes
  friction        a capability gap or protocol misfit — and the explicit empty form, for the sittings where nothing blocked you
  help            Help about any command
  inquiry-support your per-round vote on whether the report still carries a direction blue proposed
  mint            turn lens findings into a graded gap on the board, when a defect is real and belongs there
  near-match      screen a candidate against the board BEFORE minting, so a reopen does not arrive as a fresh gap
  position        your round narrative — the argument the other side answers, rendered as this round's RED section
  register        your first act at the seat, and the one call that needs your seat id — nothing else runs until it does
  regrade         move a grade on a gap that already exists, with the reason it moved
  spot-check      sample the closure archive — a duty every round owes, including the rounds with nothing to sample
  verdict         the seat's terminal act: the PASS or FAIL, and the checkpoint that follows it

Command groups — each holds commands THIS page does not list:
  class           the gap-class registry: what KINDS of defect this run recognises
  motion          file and rule on a motion — a grade dispute, a petition, or a ruling on a direction. One mechanism, one id.
  show            read a projection of the record — the tool is the read path, and the .md files are for human verification. Bare, it answers with YOUR PENDING WORK

Flags:
  -h, --help               help for feov-record
      --json               emit a structured JSON result (and structured errors) instead of human text
      --run string         the run directory. The PreToolUse hook injects it in a real run, which is why you rarely type it. A value that DISAGREES with the run you were dispatched into is refused rather than obeyed
      --seat-id register   your seat id, as the dispatch prompt states it (SEAT_ID). You pass it ONCE, at register, which binds it to you on the record; after that every call resolves it for you and typing it is optional. It SELECTS this surface — the verbs listed are the ones your seat may run — and a value disagreeing with what you registered as is refused rather than obeyed
  -v, --version            version for feov-record

Use "feov-record [command] --help" for more information about a command.

